{"content_hash": "5cd1923b2803c18f", "version_id": 699, "article_id": 70, "level_code": "ja_n2", "lang": "ja", "level": 4, "level_label": "N2 中高級", "title": "フランス各地で暴動、1200人逮捕　学校と生活費への抗議が激化", "title_zh": "法国多地爆发骚乱，1200人被捕，学校和生活费抗议升级", "has_translation": true, "topic": "world", "source": "bbc_world", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6d937wedj7jo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1485504750689-aa2121ffe6c6?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8M3x8dmlvbGVudCUyMGNsYXNoZXMlMjBsb290aW5nfGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTIyNzkxMjd8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Pawel Janiak on Unsplash", "author": "Pawel Janiak", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@pawelj?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/fire-burning-on-the-road-with-high-rise-buildings-during-daytime-photography-49LBMXrY5BE?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(36, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(74, 46%, 48%)", "label": "WORLD", "seed": "f2043e6acb50"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-18", "word_count": 269, "reading_minutes": 0.8, "lead": "フランスで18日、学校の劣悪な環境や生活費の高騰に抗議するデモが各地で行われ、暴力的な衝突や略奪が発生した。政府によると少なくとも1200人が逮捕され、警察官150人が負傷した。", "lead_zh": "18日，法国各地举行抗议学校恶劣环境和生活成本上涨的示威，发生暴力冲突和抢劫。据政府称，至少1200人被捕，150名警察受伤。", "preview": "フランス全土で18日、学校の環境悪化や生活費の高騰に反対するデモが行われ、約55万人が街頭に集まった。政府は「暴力の激化」と表現し、少なくとも1200人が逮捕された。パリでは夜まで機動隊と激しく衝突し、催涙ガスや放水が使われた。", "preview_zh": "18日，法国各地举行反对学校环境恶化和生活成本上涨的示威，约55万人走上街头。政府称这是“暴力升级”，至少1200人被捕。在巴黎，示威者与防暴警察冲突持续到夜晚，警方使用了催泪瓦斯和高压水枪。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 687, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/70/ja_n2.mp3", "duration": 51.575, "size_bytes": 308880, "engine": "kokoro", "voice": "jf_alpha", "word_count": 181, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@0da0f65/content/data/versions/699.json", "paragraphs": ["フランス全土で18日、学校の環境悪化や生活費の高騰に反対するデモが行われ、約55万人が街頭に集まった。政府は「暴力の激化」と表現し、少なくとも1200人が逮捕された。パリでは夜まで機動隊と激しく衝突し、催涙ガスや放水が使われた。", "首都パリや南西部リモージュでは建物が放火され、リモージュの市庁舎は大火で屋根の一部が崩落した。複数の都市で略奪が発生し、市庁舎や商店が破壊された。リヨンでは観光案内所が焼失し、市長は「悲劇だ」と述べた。サンテティエンヌでは若い男性が手榴弾で手を失う事故も起きた。", "パリの主要デモは午後にはおおむね平穏だったが、日が進むにつれて一部の集団が車を焼き、店舗を荒らした。"], "paragraphs_zh": ["18日，法国各地举行反对学校环境恶化和生活成本上涨的示威，约55万人走上街头。政府称这是“暴力升级”，至少1200人被捕。在巴黎，示威者与防暴警察冲突持续到夜晚，警方使用了催泪瓦斯和高压水枪。", "首都巴黎和西南部利摩日有建筑被纵火，利摩日市政厅因大火部分屋顶坍塌。多个城市发生抢劫，市政厅和商店遭到破坏。里昂旅游局被烧毁，市长称这是“悲剧”。圣艾蒂安还发生一名年轻男子被手榴弹炸断手的事故。", "巴黎的主要示威下午基本和平，但随着时间推移，一些团体烧毁车辆、洗劫店铺。防暴警察冲入人群，用警棍殴打多人。内政部称这是“戴兜帽的人”实施的有针对性暴力。"], "body": "フランス全土で18日、学校の環境悪化や生活費の高騰に反対するデモが行われ、約55万人が街頭に集まった。政府は「暴力の激化」と表現し、少なくとも1200人が逮捕された。パリでは夜まで機動隊と激しく衝突し、催涙ガスや放水が使われた。\n\n首都パリや南西部リモージュでは建物が放火され、リモージュの市庁舎は大火で屋根の一部が崩落した。複数の都市で略奪が発生し、市庁舎や商店が破壊された。リヨンでは観光案内所が焼失し、市長は「悲劇だ」と述べた。サンテティエンヌでは若い男性が手榴弾で手を失う事故も起きた。\n\nパリの主要デモは午後にはおおむね平穏だったが、日が進むにつれて一部の集団が車を焼き、店舗を荒らした。", "body_zh": "18日，法国各地举行反对学校环境恶化和生活成本上涨的示威，约55万人走上街头。政府称这是“暴力升级”，至少1200人被捕。在巴黎，示威者与防暴警察冲突持续到夜晚，警方使用了催泪瓦斯和高压水枪。\n\n首都巴黎和西南部利摩日有建筑被纵火，利摩日市政厅因大火部分屋顶坍塌。多个城市发生抢劫，市政厅和商店遭到破坏。里昂旅游局被烧毁，市长称这是“悲剧”。圣艾蒂安还发生一名年轻男子被手榴弹炸断手的事故。\n\n巴黎的主要示威下午基本和平，但随着时间推移，一些团体烧毁车辆、洗劫店铺。防暴警察冲入人群，用警棍殴打多人。内政部称这是“戴兜帽的人”实施的有针对性暴力。", "text": "フランス全土で18日、学校の環境悪化や生活費の高騰に反対するデモが行われ、約55万人が街頭に集まった。政府は「暴力の激化」と表現し、少なくとも1200人が逮捕された。パリでは夜まで機動隊と激しく衝突し、催涙ガスや放水が使われた。 首都パリや南西部リモージュでは建物が放火され、リモージュの市庁舎は大火で屋根の一部が崩落した。複数の都市で略奪が発生し、市庁舎や商店が破壊された。リヨンでは観光案内所が焼失し、市長は「悲劇だ」と述べた。サンテティエンヌでは若い男性が手榴弾で手を失う事故も起きた。 パリの主要デモは午後にはおおむね平穏だったが、日が進むにつれて一部の集団が車を焼き、店舗を荒らした。", "vocab": [{"word": "高騰", "pos": "noun", "zh": "高涨、飙升", "note": "多用于物价、费用上涨", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "機動隊", "pos": "noun", "zh": "防暴警察", "note": "日本也指 riot police", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "催涙ガス", "pos": "noun", "zh": "催泪瓦斯", "note": "示威报道常用词", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "放火", "pos": "noun", "zh": "纵火", "note": "动词形为「放火する」", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "崩落", "pos": "noun", "zh": "坍塌", "note": "建筑、屋顶等塌落", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "略奪", "pos": "noun", "zh": "抢劫、掠夺", "note": "比「強盗」更强调趁乱抢夺", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "焼失", "pos": "noun", "zh": "烧毁", "note": "建筑被火烧掉", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "突入", "pos": "noun", "zh": "冲入、闯入", "note": "「群衆に突入する」", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "警棒", "pos": "noun", "zh": "警棍", "note": "警察使用的棍棒", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "押し付ける", "pos": "verb", "zh": "强加、强迫", "note": "「意見を押し付ける」", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "訴追", "pos": "noun", "zh": "起诉、追诉", "note": "法律用语，正式表达", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "老朽化", "pos": "noun", "zh": "老化、陈旧", "note": "设施、建筑年久失修", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "拡大", "pos": "noun", "zh": "扩大", "note": "规模、范围变大", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "補習教員", "pos": "noun", "zh": "辅导教师", "note": "补充教学人手", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "Violent clashes, looting and buildings ablaze in France as over 1,000 arrested after protests", "summary_original": "Disorder broke out in cities across the country on a day in which more than half a million joined cost of living protests.", "body_original": "Violent clashes, looting and buildings ablaze in France as over 1,000 arrested after protests\nBy\nJack Burgess\nPublished\n17 October 2026, 19:40 BST\nUpdated 2 hours ago\nViolence broke out across France on Saturday during the latest day of demonstrations against hardship in schools and the cost of living.\nAt least 1,200 people were arrested during what the French government described as an \"escalation in violence\" alongside an estimated 550,000 taking to the streets.\nIn Paris, there were significant clashes into the evening with riot police, who used tear gas and water cannon on crowds.\nBuildings were set alight in the capital and other areas, including in Limoges where a large fire in the town hall caused the roof to partly collapse.\nLooting broke out in several cities, with widespread vandalism targeting city halls and businesses also reported.\nPrime Minister Sébastien Lecornu said 150 police officers were injured in the unrest.\nIn Paris, the main march appeared to be largely peaceful during the afternoon. A group of young people told the BBC they were \"pacifists\" who are \"just trying to make things change, but nothing is moving\".\nHowever, as the day wore on some groups lit fires in the street and torched vehicles, including in iconic locations in the city centre like the Place de la République.\nShops were ransacked, at least one restaurant was gutted by fire, and the BBC saw fighting breaking out among some of the groups.\nRiot police were seen charging at one crowd in central Paris and hitting several people with batons.\nIn Lyon, Mayor Grégory Doucet said the burning of the city's tourist office was \"a tragedy\" for the city, telling BFMTV \"it breaks our hearts because it's a very iconic, well-known historic building\".\nLocal police said \"hostile individuals\" prevented firefighters from safely tackling the blaze.\nFire crews also battled the fire at Limoges town hall, which the local prefecture said caused part of the building to collapse.\nA young man \"had his hand blown off by a grenade\" in Saint-Étienne, the south-eastern city's Mayor Régis Juanico said on social media, adding: \"Such a tragedy should never have happened.\"\nThe interior ministry said the protests involved \"targeted acts of violence\" from \"hooded individuals\" in places, including parts of the capital and also Marseille, Rennes, Toulouse and Angers.\nDamage to buildings was reported across France, including in Grenoble, Avignon, Pau, Montpellier and Valence.\nClothes and food shops were raided in Paris, while an Apple store in Lille was broken into and emptied.\nFootage authenticated by BBC Verify showed a tourist train in Grenoble being driven by masked men along a narrow street in the city centre towards at least three riot police officers.\nHundreds of thousands of students have protested in recent weeks over staff shortages and dilapidated facilities in the country's lycées - secondary schools attended by 15 to 18-year-olds.\nOn Saturday, their numbers were bolstered by trade union members and other protest groups.\nThese groups include the so-called gilets jaunes 'yellow vest' movement, who demonstrated against cost-of-living hikes for over a year from 2018 - becoming one of the longest-lived protest movements in French history.\nWhile France is no stranger to outbreaks of protest and disorder, this round comes as the country heads into a period of deep political uncertainty.\nFrench President Emmanuel Macron will leave office next year and polls suggest April's presidential election could come down to a fight between the leader of the National Rally, Marine Le Pen, and Jean-Luc Mélenchon of the hard-left La France Insoumise party.\nThe latter took part in demonstrations in France and later accused police officers of \"unleashing\" on protesters, while condemning looting and arson.\nPrime Minister Lecornu said his comments were \"dangerous and cynical\".\nHe earlier said police had faced \"violence of extreme intensity\" and some groups were using the protests as a \"warm-up\" for the presidential elections, adding: \"No-one will impose their political agenda through violence.\"\nLe Pen said \"legitimate demands\" voiced by protesters had been \"held hostage by the far left\", accusing Mélenchon of fuelling the violence.\nFrench President Emmanuel Macron said: \"Those who have broken, attacked the prefectures as well as businesses, looted even our town halls, will be prosecuted and punished.\"\nThe government has made apparent attempts at concessions, with Education Minister Édouard Geffray promising 3,000 extra supply teachers, during a television interview on 8 October.\nHowever, the protests have continued and intensified.\nRelated topics\nEurope\nFrance\nMore on this story\nWatch: 'Mood has really shifted' as Paris protesters clash with police\nPublishe